came US citizen 2006. From 1999 Wimbledon women's doubles: she and Elena Tatarkova lost in semifinals. From 1998 Boston Cup – Singles: she won final vs Barbara Schett. From 1998 Boston Cup – Doubles: she was runner-up with Mary Joe Fernández.\n\nThus answer: Serena has far more Grand Slam singles titles (23 vs none), more Wimbledon singles titles (7 vs none), held world No.1 ranking, multiple Olympic gold medals, etc. Mariaan's achievements limited to one WTA singles title and a Wimbledon doubles semifinal.\n\nProvide concise answer and citations.\n\nNeed JSON with answer string and citations list of [title, sentence_index].\n\nSelect appropriate citations:\n\n- Serena Grand Slam singles: \"Williams sisters\", sentence_id 0.\n- Serena Wimbledon singles titles: \"Williams sisters\", sentence_id 3.\n- Serena No.1 ranking: \"Williams sisters\", sentence_id 9.\n- Serena Olympic gold medals: \"Williams sisters\", sentence_id 6.\n- Mariaan de Swardt professional and Olympics: \"Mariaan de Swardt\", sentence_id 0 and 1.\n- Mariaan Wimbledon doubles semifinal: \"1999 Wimbledon Championships – Women's Doubles\", sentence_id 2.\n- Mariaan WTA singles title: \"1998 Boston Cup – Singles\", sentence_id 0.\n\nNow craft answer: \"Serena Williams has won 23 Grand Slam singles titles, seven Wimbledon singles titles, held the world No. 1 singles ranking, won multiple Olympic gold medals, and has a long record of Grand Slam finals, whereas Mariaan de Swardt’s career includes a single WTA singles title and a Wimbledon doubles semifinal, with no Grand Slam singles titles.\" Provide citations.\n\nReturn JSON."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1347,"completion_tokens":816,"total_tokens":2163,"audio_prompt_tokens":0},"created":1791990019,"object":"chat.completion","prompt_filter_results":null}